Vulkan: one submission and one wait per present, and a kept readback buffer.

- The engine's present was three submissions and three fence waits: the blit onto the display image, a full-frame
  readback whose only reader is the centre-pixel debug hook (and the PPM dump), and the window blit. The blit and a
  centre-pixel copy (the whole frame only when it is dumped) now go into the frame's batch, which is submitted
  as it is; the swapchain blit is a second command buffer that waits for the acquire, and one fence covers both.
- vk_eng_readback created, mapped and freed a host buffer per call; a title copying its picture to main memory
  reads 3.6 MB back every frame. The staging buffer is now kept and grown.

---
